.TH SIMPLE_SHELL 1 "" "Simple Shell" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
simple_shell - a simple UNIX command interpreter

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./simple_shell

.SH DESCRIPTION
simple_shell reads commands from standard input and executes them using
fork and execve.

.PP
The shell supports commands with arguments and searches for executable
commands using the PATH environment variable.

.PP
It works in interactive and non-interactive mode.

.SH BUILTIN COMMANDS
.TP
.B exit
Exits the shell.

.TP
.B env
Prints the current environment.

.SH USAGE
Run the shell with:

.nf
$ ./hsh
($) ls
($) ls -l
($) env
($) exit
.fi

.SH PATH
Commands are searched for using the PATH environment variable.
Commands containing a slash are executed using the specified path.

.SH EOF
Ctrl-D (EOF) exits the shell cleanly.

.SH ERRORS
If a command cannot be found, an error message is printed.

